# GRC Controls Assessment 

## Framework
NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0

## Purpose
Document the Azure security controls implemented in the Team Thomas LLC lab, their relationship to NIST CSF 2.0, and their verification status.

## Control Register

| Control ID | Security Control | NIST CSF Category | Purpose | Verification Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|

| C-01 | Microsoft Entra ID and Azure RBAC | PR.AA — Identity Management, Authentication, and Access Control | Restrict employee access using least privilege | Partially verified — Entra group membership confirmed; intended group RBAC assignment not verified |

#C-01 identity and access control assessment

**Implementation:** Created the GRP-Azure-Employees security group and configured Azure RBAC permissions in the lab.

**Evidence:** Entra group membership was confirmed. Azure IAM showed Reader assignments for two lab users, but the GRP-Azure-Employees group was not found during the Check access search.

**Limitation:** The Azure free trial expired before the group role assignment and effective permissions could be fully verified.

**Recommended action:** When Azure access is available, verify the group's Reader role assignment at the intended resource group scope and review effective permissions for its members. 

| C-02 | Azure Storage Data Protection | PR.DS — Data Security | Protect stored customer information through encryption, restricted network access, and secure connections | Partially verified — configuration observed; effectiveness testing incomplete |

#C-02 Azure Storage data protection assessment

**Implementation:** Configured Azure Storage with Microsoft-managed encryption, disabled public network access, an approved private endpoint, secure transfer required, and anonymous blob access disabled.

**Evidence:** Storage security settings and private endpoint approval were observed during lab configuration.

**Limitation:** End-to-end access testing was not completed before the Azure free trial expired.

**Recommended action:** When Azure access is restored, verify storage access through the private endpoint, test that public access is blocked, and review identity-based data permissions.

| C-03 | Security Logging and Monitoring | DE.CM — Continuous Monitoring | Record Azure management activity and support detection of suspicious resource changes | Partially verified — log ingestion confirmed; Sentinel alert generation not tested |

## C-03 Assessment Notes

**Implementation:** Configured Azure subscription Activity Logs to forward to Log Analytics and connected Microsoft Sentinel to the workspace. Created and enabled a scheduled analytics rule to detect successful Azure resource deletion operations.

**Evidence:** A resource group tag update appeared in the subscription Activity Log, and Azure Activity records were observed in Log Analytics using KQL. The Sentinel analytics rule was confirmed as enabled.

**Limitation:** A matching deletion event was not tested, so successful alert and incident generation remain unverified. The rule covers resource deletion operations, not all suspicious Azure activity.

**Recommended action:** When Azure access is available, test the rule with a controlled event, verify alert and incident creation, and review additional detection requirements.
